        "rhea_links": [],
        "annotation_comments": [
          {
            "type": "function",
            "text": "A type II topoisomerase that negatively supercoils closed circular double-stranded (ds) DNA in an ATP-dependent manner to modulate DNA topology and maintain chromosomes in an underwound state. Negative supercoiling favors strand separation, and DNA replication, transcription, recombination and repair, all of which involve strand separation. Also able to catalyze the interconversion of other topological isomers of dsDNA rings, including catenanes and knotted rings. Type II topoisomerases break and join 2 DNA strands simultaneously in an ATP-dependent manner.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"function\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"1\">A type II topoisomerase that negatively supercoils closed circular double-stranded (ds) DNA in an ATP-dependent manner to modulate DNA topology and maintain chromosomes in an underwound state. Negative supercoiling favors strand separation, and DNA replication, transcription, recombination and repair, all of which involve strand separation. Also able to catalyze the interconversion of other topological isomers of dsDNA rings, including catenanes and knotted rings. Type II topoisomerases break and join 2 DNA strands simultaneously in an ATP-dependent manner.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "catalytic activity",
            "text": "ATP-dependent breakage, passage and rejoining of double-stranded DNA.; EC:5.6.2.2",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"catalytic activity\">\n        <ns0:reaction evidence=\"1\">\n            <ns0:text>ATP-dependent breakage, passage and rejoining of double-stranded DNA.</ns0:text>\n            <ns0:dbReference type=\"EC\" id=\"5.6.2.2\" />\n        </ns0:reaction>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "subunit",
            "text": "Heterotetramer, composed of two GyrA and two GyrB chains. In the heterotetramer, GyrA contains the active site tyrosine that forms a transient covalent intermediate with DNA, while GyrB binds cofactors and catalyzes ATP hydrolysis.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"subunit\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"1\">Heterotetramer, composed of two GyrA and two GyrB chains. In the heterotetramer, GyrA contains the active site tyrosine that forms a transient covalent intermediate with DNA, while GyrB binds cofactors and catalyzes ATP hydrolysis.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "subcellular location",
            "text": "Cytoplasm",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"subcellular location\">\n        <ns0:subcellularLocation>\n            <ns0:location evidence=\"1\">Cytoplasm</ns0:location>\n        </ns0:subcellularLocation>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "miscellaneous",
            "text": "Few gyrases are as efficient as E.coli at forming negative supercoils. Not all organisms have 2 type II topoisomerases; in organisms with a single type II topoisomerase this enzyme also has to decatenate newly replicated chromosomes.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"miscellaneous\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"1\">Few gyrases are as efficient as E.coli at forming negative supercoils. Not all organisms have 2 type II topoisomerases; in organisms with a single type II topoisomerase this enzyme also has to decatenate newly replicated chromosomes.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "similarity",
            "text": "Belongs to the type II topoisomerase GyrA/ParC subunit family.",
